{
  "_comment": "A4 (review 2026-10-10): the one station_config parse rule, shared by the phone station (app/src/stationconfig.js parseStationConfig) and the Stick (hardware/m5sticks3/station_link.h parse_station_config); rules agreed by brx4 (app and Stick) and brx3 (MC). A refused config changes nothing on the station. Otherwise `expect` is the parsed assignment: kind, team (0-3, or 255 for any), id, game (one byte), valid_ids (integer entries in 1..65535, the first 32, or null when absent), lock_s (whole seconds, 0-7200) and has_item (an object item on a powerup station). JSON \\u escapes are out of scope (the Stick's json_lite does not decode them, and MC's json.dumps never writes one for ASCII). An infinite lock_s (JSON 1e400) locks for the cap on both. The threshold, tx_power and their ages are out of scope: each platform resolves its own default. Read by app/test/station-config-cases.test.mjs and hardware/m5sticks3/test/test_station_config_cases.cpp (via mcp/tests/test_sticks3_core.py).",
